  "commentary": {
    "market_commentary": "The SSY Pacific Capesize Index weakened throughout the holidays to be down 44 points over the past three weeks to 7,164 points. With slight weakening in iron ore demand as a result of the upcoming Chinese New Year, SSY’s assessed Australia-China iron ore spot voyage rate is $1.20/t lower over the past three weeks at $10.00/t. Despite being down, $4.90/t since mid-December, the voyage rate is up $2.85/t from same time last year. Correspondingly, the Pacific roundvoyage rate is also down $6,000/day to $20,750/day.",
    "index_notes": "The Pacific Capesize Index started at 5,000 points on 27 December 1995 and has since been subject to periodic updating to reflect changing trade patterns. The latest update was on",
    "contact_info": "For more information please contact David Beard/Roar Adland"
  },
